  ref GUE / GOE / Poisson, matched N, 2000 samples, seed 20260927
  S1 verdict: in-Poisson-only -> POISSON; in-RMT-only -> RMT;
      in both -> NO DISCRIMINATION; in neither -> INCONSISTENT
  S2 verdict: p_GUE = P(chi2_GUE >= chi2_obs),
      p_Pois = P(chi2_Pois <= chi2_obs)  [LOWER tail -- amendment
      #1001631, registered before any real spectrum was read];
      p_GUE>=0.05 & p_Pois<0.05 -> MONTGOMERY/GUE, distinguishable
      from Poisson; both >=0.05 -> NO DISCRIMINATION; p_GUE<0.05 ->
      INCONSISTENT. Must hold on ALL 6 grid points {T,L} x {0.3,0.5,1.0},
      else UNSTABLE. Threshold 0.05, bins, sigma_e, grid, seed UNCHANGED.
  EXPECTED (pre-registered): GOE-vs-GUE NOT separable at N=401;
      spread ~295 orders -> chart L non-uniform; ~200 pairs/bin.
SCOPE: this is NOT Montgomery's theorem about zeta zeros and NOT an
       RH / Weil-positivity / prime-counting / factoring claim.

